{"resourceIdentifier":"2343","resourceName":"Zhanjiang Mangrove Afforestation Project","description":"Zhanjiang Mangrove Afforestation Project (hereafter as 'the project') is located in Zhanjiang City, Guangdong Province of China, whose aim is to increase carbon sequestration and contribute to local sustainable development by planting mangroves on the degraded mangrove habitats.\r\nThe purpose of the project is to restore the degraded local mangrove ecosystem and increase forest cover by planting a variety of species of native mangrove, and establish a healthy local ecological and economic system by involving local residents into the projects implementation directly. Totally 380.40 ha of mangroves has been planted with 4 native mangroves species (Kandelia obovata, Aegiceras corniculatum, Avicennia marina and Rhizophora stylosa ). The implementation of the afforestation project will generate GHG emission removals and improve the local environment, enhance the capabilities of local communities and residents by providing them with relevant technical skills and training. In addition, the project restored the degraded mangrove ecosystem and increased forest cover, provided more suitable habitat for animals, especially for endangered birds which mainly live in mangroves.\r\nThe project is estimated to generate GHG emission removals of 106,781 tCO2e in 40 years, with an average annual GHG emission removal of 4,020 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":21.014077,"longitude":110.209333},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2020-09-08","endExclusive":"2020-10-09","endInclusive":"2020-10-08"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2343"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangdong Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Third Institute of Oceanography, Ministry of Natural Resources"},{"type":